# CHAPTER II

## OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

## OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT

Article The Regional Government is responsible for guaranteeing and making maximum efforts to respect Women and Children in accordance with their dignity without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnicity, culture and language, legal status and physical and mental condition.
1ll1- Article The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to provide protection for Women and Children in the Region.

Article The obligations and responsibilities for the implementation of Protection of Women and Children as referred to in Article 7, are carried out by the Agency.

Article The implementation of protection for Women and Children in addition to being carried out by the Agency, is also the obligation and responsibility of related Regional Apparatus that handle Government affairs, as follows: Education;

Health;

Social Affairs;

Population and Civil Registration;

Population Control and Family Planning; Manpower;

Public Order and Peace;

Cooperatives and SMEs;

1. Trade and Industry;

Transportation; and Sub-district.

# CHAPTER III

## RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

## Part One
12- Rights of Women

#### Article 10

Every Woman has the following rights:
a. b.  f. to live in prosperous conditions physically and mentally; to live in a family within the bonds of a lawful marriage in accordance with the teachings of the religion she adheres to;

to obtain education and teaching in all types, levels and pathways of education;

to obtain protection from acts of discrimination; to obtain protection from economic and sexual exploitation;

to obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence, and neglect;

to obtain decent work based on ability, interest and talent while upholding all matters related to her human nature;

to obtain access in advancing the business she undertakes in order to create an adequate increase in income;

to obtain work leave while receiving wages/income in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

to receive special protection in the performance of work or profession against matters that may threaten safety and/or health in relation to the reproductive function of Women,
k. to obtain legal information and services in accordance with her needs;
13- to enjoy a good and healthy living environment in accordance with the standards and provisions of laws and regulations;

to own and manage joint property in a lawful marriage in accordance with laws and regulations; and to have other rights attached in accordance with her human dignity based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

## Part Two

Rights of Children

#### Article 11

Every Child has the following rights:
a. the right to live, grow and develop properly in accordance with human dignity, to participate in all fields of life,; to obtain protection from acts of discrimination; to obtain protection from economic and sexual exploitation;

to obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence and neglect;

population identity and citizenship status;
f. to obtain a birth certificate;
g. to embrace religion and worship according to the teachings of religion and belief with the guidance of parents/guardians;

not to be forced to change religion by foster parents, adoptive parents and by anyone;

to be recognized and know their parents, to be raised and cared for by their own parents;
k. -14- to obtain health services and social security in accordance with physical, mental, spiritual, and social needs;

to obtain education and teaching in accordance with interests and talents;

to obtain care, education, training, self-improvement and the ability to participate in community and state life for Children with physical, mental disabilities and special needs;

to express and have their opinions heard;

to rest and utilize leisure time for self-development outside school hours;

to obtain other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

## Part Three

Special Rights for Persons with Disabilities

#### Article 12

Women and Children with disabilities, have the right to: receive various facilities in carrying out
a. various public services; and receive additional facilities and infrastructure inb. carrying out activities in public spaces.

# CHAPTER IV

## IMPROVEMENT OF QUALITY OF LIFE

## OF WOMEN IN THE REGION

## Part One
15- Paragraph Gender Mainstreaming Working Group

#### Article 13

To ensure the sustainable implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Region, the Mayor establishes a Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group.

#### Article 14

The membership of the Gender Mainstreaming Working Group as referred to in Article 13, consists of:
a. Regional Apparatus that administers Government Affairs in the field of Regional Development Planning as Chair of the Gender Mainstreaming Working Group.

Regional Apparatus that administers Government Affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment, Child Protection and Community Empowerment as Head of the Secretariat of the Gender Mainstreaming Working Group.

Regional Apparatus other than as referred to in letter and letter as members of the Gender Mainstreaming Working Group.

#### Article 15

The establishment of the Gender Mainstreaming Working Group as referred to in Article 14 is stipulated by Mayor's Decree.

Paragraph Establishment of Gender Mainstreaming Working Group at Regional Apparatus Level

#### Article 16

For the purpose of accelerating the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Region through the Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group established by the Mayor -16- as referred to in Article 25, the Mayor through the Regional Secretary orders that every head of Regional Apparatus establish a Gender Mainstreaming Working Group in each Regional Apparatus that they lead.

## Part Two

Women's Empowerment Paragraph Purpose of Women's Empowerment

#### Article 17

In order to improve the role and position as well as the quality of Women in family and society, the Regional Government carries out empowerment of Women.

#### Article 18

Women's Empowerment as referred to in Article 17 is intended so that every Woman has the ability and capacity to achieve progress in the economic, political, social, cultural, and legal fields.

Paragraph Women's Empowerment System

#### Article 19

Women's Empowerment as referred to in Article 18 is implemented through an empowerment system carried out comprehensively, inclusively and integratively.

#### Article 20

The Women's empowerment system aims to: os -17-
a. improve the quality of life of Women, and Families; b. improve the institutional capacity of Women's empowerment in the Region, including the development of its gender system; andc. provide protection for Women's rights from various forms of violence and other discriminatory treatment.

#### Article 21

In order to realize the goal of improving the quality of life of Women, and families as referred to in Article 20 letter is carried out through:
a. providing access to Women to enjoy education, health services, and other strategic fields;
b. encouraging the involvement of Women in the development process;
c. providing knowledge, skills, character values, morals, and family resilience;
d. encouraging programs that can increase the independence of Women in the economic, political, legal, social, cultural fields, as well as other strategic fields; ande. providing opportunities and chances to every Woman to occupy various positions and posts in various fields of work, including strategic positions as long as they are in accordance with their capacity and ability.

