## SPECIAL PROTECTION FOR CHILDREN

## Part One

Implementation of Special Protection for Children

#### Article 166

Implementation of special protection for Children is carried out through:
a. b. prevention of violence against Children;  

provision of services for Children requiring special protection through coordination of parties from government and non-government institutions in the Region; and strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Children requiring special protection.

#### Article 167

Special Protection for Children as referred to in Article 166 letter is provided to: Children in emergency situations;  
a. Children in conflict with the law;  

Children from minority and isolated groups;  
c. Children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;  

Children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic, and other addictive substance abuse and/or involved in their production/distribution;  

Children who are victims of pornography;  
f. Children with HIV/AIDS;  
g. Children who are victims of kidnapping, sale and/or trafficking in persons;  

Children who are victims of physical and/or psychological Violence;  

Children who are victims of sexual crimes;  
k. Children who are victims of terrorism networks;  

Children with Disabilities;  

Children who are victims of abuse and neglect;  

Children with deviant social behavior; and Children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to their Parents' condition.

#### Article 168

Special Protection for Children as referred to in Article 167 is carried out through efforts of: rapid response;  
a. medical treatment;  

physical rehabilitation;  

psychological rehabilitation;  

social rehabilitation;  

prevention of disease and other health disorders;  
f. psychosocial assistance during treatment untilg. recovery;  

provision of social assistance for Children from underprivileged Families; and provision of protection and assistance in every judicial process.

## Part Two

Protection for Child Victims of Violence Paragraph Children in Emergency Situations

#### Article 169

Children in emergency situations as referred to in Article 167 letter consist of:
a. Children who become refugees;  

Children who are victims of unrest;  

Children who are victims of natural disasters; and Children in armed conflict situations.

#### Article 170

Special Protection for Children in emergency situations who become refugees as referred to in Article 169 letter is carried out with the following provisions:
a. b. for Children who become refugees is implemented in accordance with humanitarian law provisions;  

for Children who are victims of unrest, victims of natural disasters, and Children in armed conflict situations as referred to in Article 169 letter b, letterc, and letter d, is implemented through:

1. fulfillment of basic needs consisting of food, clothing, housing, education, health, learning and recreation, security guarantees, and equal treatment; and fulfillment of special needs for Children with disabilities and Children experiencing psychosocial disorders.  

Paragraph Children in Conflict with the Law

#### Article 171

Special Protection for Children in conflict with the law as referred to in Article 167 letter is carried out through:
a. f. g.  k. 1, humane treatment with attention to needs according to their age;  

separation from adults;  

provision of legal aid and other assistance effectively;  

implementation of recreational activities;  

freedom from torture, punishment or other treatment that is cruel, inhuman and degrading to dignity and status;  

avoidance of imposition of death penalty and/or life imprisonment;  

avoidance of detention or imprisonment, except as a last resort for the shortest possible time; provision of justice before a Children's court that is objective, impartial, and in closed hearings to the public;  

avoidance of publication of their identity; provision of assistance from Parents/Guardians and persons trusted by the Child;  

provision of social advocacy;  

provision of private life;  

provision of accessibility, especially for Children with Disabilities;  

provision of education;  

provision of health services;and provision of other rights in accordance with statutory provisions.  

Paragraph Children from Minority and Isolated Groups

#### Article 172

Special Protection for Children from minority and isolated groups as referred to in Article 167 letter is carried out through:
a. b. provision of infrastructure and facilities to be able to enjoy their own culture;  

acknowledge and practice their own religion; and use their own language.  

Paragraph Children Who Are Economically Exploited

#### Article 173

