a. dissemination and/or socialization of statutory provisions related to Protection of Children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;  

monitoring, reporting, and imposition of sanctions; and involvement of various companies, labor unions, non-governmental organizations, and the Community in eliminating exploitation of Children economically and/or sexually.  

Paragraph Children Who Are Victims of Narcotics, Alcohol, Psychotropic, and Other Addictive Substance Abuse

#### Article 174

